<title>USA: Taitron Components sets stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Taitron Components sets stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taitron Components Inc on Tuesday said its board of directors has authorized the repurchase of up to $1.0 million worth of its common stock from time to time in open market transactions.</p>
<p>This follows the recent completion of a previously announced stock repurchase program, under which the company purchased roughly $631,000 worth of its common stock.  The stock purchases will be financed through available cash.</p>
<p>Taitron, a distributor of transistors, diodes and other discrete semiconductors, has about 6.8 million shares outstanding.</p>
</text>
